# M14: a paste is one undo step (CORE-43). Three paragraphs are typed, selected and copied; the caret goes to the end and Paste adds them
# again (six paragraphs), and one Edit > Undo takes the whole paste back (three paragraphs), where it used to take one paragraph at a time.
o n e enter t w o enter t h r e e
f10 right l                     # Edit > Select All
f10 right c                     # Edit > Copy
end                             # the caret to the end, the selection gone
f10 right p                     # Edit > Paste: one, two, three, one, two, three
f10 right u                     # Edit > Undo: the whole paste goes
f10 right r                     # Edit > Redo: all of it is back
f10 right u                     # and gone again
f10 end enter                   # File > Exit
n                               # without saving
